27 claims; 0 removal(s).
  run_ids: null -> ["6a39faa6-e685-4b93-891d-df53c89e2ba8"]
  crate: null -> "bit_field"
  version: null -> "0.10.3"
  title: null -> "Integer single-bit operations and generic slice routing, with exact failure cases"
  explanation: null -> "The unchanged bit_field 0.10.3 single-bit methods are verified for all twelve integer types: in-range indices read or update exactly that bit, returned mutable-reference writes propagate to the original value, and invalid indices fail at the assertion. All twelve primitive BIT_LENGTH values equal their widths. The original generic slice bit_length/get_bit/set_bit bodies are also composition-proved: assuming their declared BitField constant and per-element normal-return contracts, they use element index bit/width and local index bit%width, preserve other slice entries on update, and report zero-width/out-of-bounds errors. bit_length returns length times width or integerOverflow. Rust source and Cargo.toml are archive-identical."
  trusted_assumptions: null -> "The official Rust/Charon/Aeneas translation and integer/slice models, Lean, and Kani/CBMC are trusted. Twelve explicit monomorphized size_of models supply the integer byte sizes on x86_64, including pointer size 8; Kani checks their actual layouts and all primitive single-bit methods/returned-reference behavior for arbitrary valid values. Connecting Kani Rust and Lean representations is a reviewed bridge, not an in-Lean std layout proof; Rust nightlies differ. Generic slice theorems assume the complete stated observation/update callback contracts, including the final state after returned-reference writeback. They do not prove arbitrary callback implementations. Mapped audits allow only propext, Classical.choice and Quot.sound."
  tool_version_id: null -> "aeneas-be86ab0f1989d04944292b345b24c435be3ad10a"
  environment: null -> "Original crates.io bit_field0.10.3; x86_64 default features, debug extraction. Rust nightly-2026-09-17, Charon08d7c9d50144bd84848212c24701253585e90d1f, Aeneas be86ab0f1989d04944292b345b24c435be3ad10a, Lean4.35.0. Official original-body extraction with primitive monomorphization and separate generic slice roots. Kani0.68.0/CBMC6.11.0/Rust nightly-2026-08-21: 24 supplementary primitive harnesses/600 checks, plus the separate concrete range observation."
  evidence_url: null -> "https://github.com/nyuichi/rust-crate-proofs/tree/acc19f974aef54ac200709255cbe40eb1de757e5"
  limitations: null -> "Only twenty-four primitive single-bit methods, twelve width constants and three callback-conditional slice bodies are established. Primitive and slice get_bits/set_bits range methods remain unproved. A separately Kani-checked example shows signed range behavior differs from ordinary masked updates: 112_i8.set_bits(0..4,1) yields 1, changing high bits outside the range; the unsigned example yields 113. The verified single-bit methods are unaffected. Generic callback side effects, failure/divergence outside the stated contracts, other targets and release extraction are not established. No generic Rust size_of property, panic text or unwinding-state guarantee is claimed."
