  "trusted_assumptions": "The official Rust/Charon/Aeneas translation and integer/slice models, Lean, and Kani/CBMC are trusted. Twelve explicit monomorphized size_of models supply the integer byte sizes on x86_64, including pointer size 8; Kani checks their actual layouts and all primitive single-bit methods/returned-reference behavior for arbitrary valid values. Connecting Kani Rust and Lean representations is a reviewed bridge, not an in-Lean std layout proof; Rust nightlies differ. Generic slice theorems assume the complete stated observation/update callback contracts, including the final state after returned-reference writeback. They do not prove arbitrary callback implementations. Mapped audits allow only propext, Classical.choice and Quot.sound.",
